<title>UK: Scotia says U.S. trials start on Foscan.</title>
<headline>Scotia says U.S. trials start on Foscan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British biotechnology firm Scotia Holdings Plc said on Tuesday its U.S. clinical trials have now started on its Foscan compound.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the first study in the U.S. was in recurrent oral cavity and pharyngeal cancers.</p>
<p>The compound was granted Investigational New Drug status from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) in December 1996.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
